00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:37.010
This is not about the
specific numbers that you see

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:39.920
but it's rather about
the overall methodology,

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:41.977
the overall logic of tracking all of this.

00:02:41.977 --> 00:02:44.210
So you see that there are two parts here.

00:02:44.210 --> 00:02:46.340
The upper part that tracks the net worth,

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:48.930
and then the lower part
that tracks the cashflow.

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:51.040
In the strict sense, the only
thing that's really relevant

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:53.000
for your net worth is this upper part.

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:55.030
Though I do believe that
for your personal finances,

00:02:55.030 --> 00:02:57.800
it is important to get an
understanding of your cashflow.

00:02:57.800 --> 00:03:00.250
So your income and your expenses as well.

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:01.760
So let's start with the net worth.

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:03.240
What is actually your net worth?

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:04.740
And the answer to that is

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:07.730
that the net worth is the
difference between your assets

00:03:07.730 --> 00:03:09.160
and your liabilities.

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:10.400
Now we are going to look together

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:11.870
into what exactly this means.

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:14.530
But the net worth pretty much
is how rich you are, right.

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:16.550
What is the value of all your holdings?

00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:17.440
What is the value

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:19.760
of everything that you
have against your name?

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:22.110
So again, looking back into
this sheet, you can see

00:03:22.110 --> 00:03:25.520
that it takes as a formula,
the sum of your assets,

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:28.260
and it subtracts the
sum of your liabilities.

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:30.090
So this is here, what the net worth is.

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:31.790
And then the growth is just tracking

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:34.280
the percentage difference, month on month.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:36.100
So let's look into these two areas,

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:37.770
assets and liabilities, in detail.

00:03:37.770 --> 00:03:39.210
Let's start with the assets.

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:41.850
So what you see here now
is a structure of assets

00:03:41.850 --> 00:03:43.700
that probably works for many people.

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:44.533
But of course,

00:03:44.533 --> 00:03:46.800
if now you track this for
yourself, just ask yourself,

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:48.650
what are the assets that you actually own?

00:03:48.650 --> 00:03:51.440
And then of course, feel
free to delete whole sections

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:53.520
or maybe even add additional sections

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:56.740
if you feel like the
specific assets that you own

00:03:56.740 --> 00:03:58.420
do not really fit in
to this scheme, right.

00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:00.090
But this is just something
that I believe is

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:02.430
generally applicable and
works for many people.

00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:04.130
So let's start with your deposits.

00:04:04.130 --> 00:04:06.420
So this is just the accounts, the accounts

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:08.920
with banks or any other
accounts that you hold,

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:10.690
they pretty much have cash on them.

00:04:10.690 --> 00:04:12.810
So in this example here, there
are two checking accounts.

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:15.370
One at the Deutsche Bank,
one at the Commerzbank.

00:04:15.370 --> 00:04:17.540
Then there is a savings account and then

00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:19.430
you might have some money on your PayPal.

00:04:19.430 --> 00:04:21.280
Again, you might have more accounts,

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:23.130
you might have fewer accounts.

00:04:23.130 --> 00:04:25.490
Just insert every account in a line,

00:04:25.490 --> 00:04:27.360
and then just track every month

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:28.930
how much money you have on it.

00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:31.920
What I personally do not
track is the cash that I have

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:33.610
with me at any point in time.

00:04:33.610 --> 00:04:36.490
So this would of course, be
part of your net worth as well.

00:04:36.490 --> 00:04:39.200
Personally, I receive this
as a little extra that I have

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:41.120
and I will not specifically
track this here.

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:42.020
So far, so good.

00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:44.800
Let's look into the next
section, financial instruments.

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:47.630
And here you can pretty
much add all the stocks,

00:04:47.630 --> 00:04:49.810
all the ETFs, all the funds,

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:52.290
all these securities that you own.

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:54.890
What exactly this is and
how many different positions

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:56.510
you have, of course can depend.

00:04:56.510 --> 00:04:58.520
So if you are interested
how I specifically think

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:00.920
about this whole investment
topic, I made a whole video

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:02.850
about investments for young professionals.

